    <statement><p>Evaluate the function at the specified points.</p>
<p><m>h(x,y,z) = x\frac{1}{y^{4}}z, \left(-2,2,3\right), \left(4,2,4\right)</m></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-2,2,3\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(4,2,4\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.375</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>(x,y,z) = \left(-2,2,3\right)</m> to find 
<m>h(-2,2,3) = -2 \cdot \frac{1}{2^{4}} \cdot 3 = \frac{-6}{16} = -0.375</m>.



For the second point, substitute <m>(x,y,z) = \left(4,2,4\right)</m> to find 
<m>h(4,2,4) = 4 \cdot \frac{1}{2^{4}} \cdot 4 = \frac{16}{16} = 1</m>.





</solution>
